{
  "id": "COMPOUND:27215 - PROTEIN:4972",
  "verbalization": "Bornyl chloride, (-)- is implicated in the regulation of LAMA-84 through a series of molecular interactions involving different compounds. The evidence suggests that Bornyl chloride, (-)- acts as a target for multiple compounds, including SNU-387, Anolobine, and Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, all of which are themselves targets of LAMA-84. This indicates a potential pathway where Bornyl chloride, (-)- may influence the activity of these compounds, which in turn affect LAMA-84. The presence of multiple targets for Bornyl chloride, (-)- suggests a possible role in modulating the biological activity of these compounds, potentially through interactions at the level of enzyme or receptor binding. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Bornyl chloride, (-)- and LAMA-84, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
